import BlogLayout from '../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro';
---
<BlogLayout
  title="2D vs 3D As-Built Drawings: Which Do You Need?"
  description="A practical decision guide. When 2D as-built drawings make sense, when a 3D Revit model is worth the cost, and how to avoid over-ordering."
  category="Article"
  readTime="6 min"
>
  <p>The single most expensive scoping mistake we see is a client paying for a 3D BIM model when 2D floor plans would have done the job, and the second most expensive is a contractor finding out mid-coordination that 2D drawings don't actually answer the question they need answered. The cost gap between those two outcomes is about 4&times;.</p>

